{"id": "tea:kramadipika:10", "source": "src:kramadipika", "location": {"ref": "10"}, "paraphrase": "The five winds: prāṇa at mouth and nose, apāna at the navel, samāna at the heart, udāna at the throat, vyāna at the joints, named from leading forth, leading down, leading together, rising and spreading.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "terms": ["trm:prana", "trm:apana", "trm:samana", "trm:udana", "trm:vyana"], "concepts": ["cpt:five-vayus"], "notes": "Kramadīpikā's own 23-sūtra numbering.", "coverage": ["A5"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U09-samkhya"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U09-samkhya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kramadipika:11", "source": "src:kramadipika", "location": {"ref": "11"}, "paraphrase": "The five agents: the vaikārika does good actions, the taijasa bad ones, the bhūtādi deluded ones; the sānumāna good-and-deluded ones, the niranumāna bad-and-deluded ones.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:karmatman"], "notes": "Kramadīpikā's own 23-sūtra numbering.", "coverage": ["A5"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U09-samkhya"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U09-samkhya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kramadipika:12", "source": "src:kramadipika", "location": {"ref": "12"}, "paraphrase": "The five-jointed avidyā: darkness (taking the eight non-selves, from the unmanifest to the subtle elements, as self), delusion (self-assertion for the eight powers), great delusion (thinking 'I am liberated' amid the ten seen and heard objects), gloom (aversion when the powers and objects are obstructed) and blind gloom (despair at death when they have been attained) — sixty-two divisions.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:tamas", "trm:moha", "trm:mahamoha", "trm:tamisra", "trm:andhatamisra"], "obstacles": ["obs:viparyaya"], "notes": "Kramadīpikā's own 23-sūtra numbering.", "coverage": ["A5"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U09-samkhya"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U09-samkhya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kramadipika:16", "source": "src:kramadipika", "location": {"ref": "16"}, "paraphrase": "The ten fundamental topics — existence (of pradhāna and puruṣa), oneness, purposiveness, being for another, otherness, non-agency, conjunction, separation, the plurality of puruṣas and the persistence of the body — are each proved by a Kārikā verse; with the fifty cognitions they are the sixty topics called Ṣaṣṭitantra.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "terms": ["trm:mulikartha", "trm:sastitantra"], "concepts": ["cpt:sastitantra-sixty-topics"], "notes": "Kramadīpikā's own 23-sūtra numbering.", "coverage": ["A5"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U09-samkhya"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U09-samkhya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kramadipika:18-19", "source": "src:kramadipika", "location": {"ref": "18-19"}, "paraphrase": "The fourteenfold creation: eight divine (daiva, paiśāca, rākṣasa, yākṣa, gāndharva, aindra, prājāpatya, brāhma), five animal (domestic animals, birds, wild beasts, reptiles, plants) and one human; the threefold creation of bodily constituents: subtle (the subtle bodies), born of mother and father (hair, blood and flesh from the mother; sinew, bone and marrow from the father) and the gross elements.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["world-fate", "body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:fourteenfold-creation", "cpt:linga-sarira"], "notes": "Kramadīpikā's own 23-sūtra numbering.", "coverage": ["A5"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U09-samkhya"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U09-samkhya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kramadipika:20", "source": "src:kramadipika", "location": {"ref": "20"}, "paraphrase": "Bondage is threefold: bondage to prakṛti (absorption in prakṛti by taking the eight prakṛtis as highest); bondage to the modifications (of renunciants and worldly people ruled by the senses and attached to objects); and bondage through gifts (of students, householders, mendicants and forest-dwellers who give gifts with self-conceit, their minds struck by desire and delusion).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:threefold-bondage-and-release"], "obstacles": ["obs:threefold-bondage", "obs:prakrtilaya"], "notes": "Kramadīpikā's own 23-sūtra numbering.", "coverage": ["A5"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U09-samkhya"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U09-samkhya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kramadipika:21", "source": "src:kramadipika", "location": {"ref": "21"}, "paraphrase": "Liberation is threefold: by the increase of knowledge, by the calming of the senses' passion, and by total exhaustion (of virtue and non-virtue), from which comes isolation.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:threefold-bondage-and-release", "cpt:kaivalya"], "notes": "Kramadīpikā's own 23-sūtra numbering.", "coverage": ["A5"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U09-samkhya"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U09-samkhya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kramadipika:22", "source": "src:kramadipika", "location": {"ref": "22"}, "paraphrase": "The means of knowledge are three; a reliable person (āpta) is one devoted to his own work, free of passion and aversion, knowing and virtuous; through the three, the principles are measured as grain by a measure.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "terms": ["trm:aptavacana"], "concepts": ["cpt:pramana"], "notes": "Kramadīpikā's own 23-sūtra numbering.", "coverage": ["A5"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U09-samkhya"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U09-samkhya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kramadipika:8", "source": "src:kramadipika", "location": {"ref": "8"}, "paraphrase": "The five functions of buddhi are: resolve (of buddhi), self-assertion (of ahaṃkāra), desire (of manas), the task of awareness (of the sense capacities) and action (of the action capacities).", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "terms": ["trm:pancabhibuddhi"], "notes": "Kramadīpikā's own 23-sūtra numbering.", "coverage": ["A5"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U09-samkhya"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U09-samkhya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kramadipika:9", "source": "src:kramadipika", "location": {"ref": "9"}, "paraphrase": "The five sources of action are steadfastness, faith, (seeking) happiness, the wish not to know and the wish to know; the first four lead to bondage, the wish to know (vividiṣā), womb of wisdom for meditators, to liberation.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "practice"], "terms": ["trm:karmayoni"], "notes": "Kramadīpikā's own 23-sūtra numbering.", "coverage": ["A5"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U09-samkhya"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U09-samkhya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kramadipika:intro", "source": "src:kramadipika", "location": {"ref": "intro"}, "paraphrase": "A brahmin overwhelmed by the threefold suffering took refuge with the Sāṃkhya teacher, the great sage Kapila, told his family, name, lineage and Vedic study, and asked: 'What is highest here, what is true, by doing what would I be fulfilled?' Kapila answered with the aphorisms.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:teacher-in-samkhya"], "teachers": ["tch:kapila"], "notes": "Kramadīpikā's own 23-sūtra numbering.", "coverage": ["A5"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U09-samkhya"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U09-samkhya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
